AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"ESFGJT\n\nA strong low pressure system off the Pacific Coast will begin to draw\nin tropical moisture associated with Topical Storm Rachel this\nweekend. This strong southerly fetch will draw anomalously high\nmoisture content across the Desert Southwest and into eastern Utah\nand western Colorado. The chance for widespread precipitation\nincreases Saturday evening into Sunday. Total precipitation forecasts\nrange from 1 to 3 inches across high terrain, with highest amounts\nfavoring the Uintas, Tavaputs and the Southwest San Juan mountains.\n\nEmbedded thunderstorms are also possible Sunday afternoon, increasing\nthe threat for flash flooding across vulnerable terrain. While\nconfidence in location and rainfall rates remain low at this time,\nthe potential for rapidly rising rivers, streams, normally dry\narroyos and slot canyons are possible Sunday through Monday.\n\nPlease follow the evolving forecast, especially if your plans\nincluding recreating or commuting across eastern Utah and western\nColorado Sunday onward. Also, keep in mind weather potential above\nyour location and upstream, particularly for those who reside below\nsensitive terrain like recent burn scars.","ends":"2026-10-12T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Delta, CO; Dolores, CO; Garfield, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO; Mesa, CO; Moffat, CO; Montezuma, CO; Montrose, CO; Ouray, CO; Rio Blanco, CO; San Juan, CO; San Miguel, CO; Daggett, UT; Grand, UT; San Juan, UT; Uintah, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-11T11:55:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 111155 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 555 AM MDT Sun Oct 11 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Deep moisture continues through the weekend as remnants of tropical system Rachel move through the region, especially overnight and through Sunday. Rainfall totals of 2-3 inches are possible over the eastern Utah mountains and 1-2 inches across the San Jua","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-11T09:00:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... Widespread wetting rains will continue across the region today, as extra-tropical moisture moves across the region. Some strong thunderstorms are expected to develop with damaging winds, hail, and heavy rainfall. Flash flooding remains a concern around sensitive terrain. Winds will increase appreciably today, gusting to around 45 mph across much of eastern UT and western CO. Critica","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":null,"aviation":{"icao":"KHDN","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"METAR KHDN 111556Z AUTO 09011KT 10SM BKN100 OVC110 13/08 A2992 RMK AO2 SLP077 T01280083","temp_f":55,"wind_dir":90,"wind_kt":11,"gust_kt":null,"visibility":"10+","cover":"OVC","flight_category":"VFR","altimeter":1013.3,"observed":1791734160,"raw_taf":"TAF KHDN 111140Z 1112/1212 11012KT P6SM -SHRA SCT040 OVC060 PROB30 1112/1115 4SM -SHRA BKN025 OVC040 FM111800 20011G20KT P6SM SCT040 BKN060 PROB30 1118/1120 4SM -SHRA BKN050 FM112000 21015G25KT P6SM VCSH SCT050 BKN070 PROB30 1120/1124 VRB22G37KT 5SM -TSRA BKN060CB FM120000 16011G22KT P6SM SCT060 BKN080 PROB30 1200/1206 4SM -SHRA BKN060 FM120600 11013G28KT P6SM SCT060 BKN090 WS020/21040KT","url":"https://aviationweather.gov/data/metar/?ids=KHDN&hours=0"},"airgradient":null,"airnow":null,"openmeteo_aq":{"pm25":3.4,"pm10":4.3,"co":107,"no2":1.1,"so2":0.2,"o3":76,"european_aqi":28,"us_aqi":32,"time":"2026-10-11T10:00"},"usgs":null,"snotel":null,"cdot_camera":{"id":"969","name":"US 40 MP 040.35 WB at Elk Spings Ranch","lat":40.37032,"lon":-108.389,"distance_km":48.7,"imageUrl":null,"pageUrl":"h